WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.930
 Your bank settings live on the brand, not

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:05.960
 on your account.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:10.240
 So, open your account, pick the brand and

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.600
 scroll down to payments and bank.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.970
 Same place on the web, same path, same

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:21.000
 account, whichever screen is nearest.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.380
 Until a bank is connected, this page does

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.200
 nothing. Balance unavailable, no payouts

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:29.200
 yet.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.170
 Accept the Mingla host terms and Stripe

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:34.760
's own pages take it from there.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.030
 Your business details, your bank details.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.960
 Mingla never sees them.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.350
 And then, you're connected to Stripe.

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:48.320
 Payments are ready for this brand.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.180
 Nigeria works differently. A brand

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.430
 belongs to one country, so for Nigeria

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:57.360
 you make a Nigerian brand.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.040
 Name it. And the address does the rest.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.810
 Put a Lagos address on a brand and Ming

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:06.360
ler has already chosen for you.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:10.480
 Nigeria. Naira. Paystack.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.600
 You can open the country list and it is

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.080
 worth seeing why.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:18.190
 Every country shows you its currency.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:21.960
 Nigeria is the only one that names its

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:21.960
 rail.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.240
 Bank transfer via Paystack.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:28.480
 And Paystack does something Stripe cannot

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.190
. No hosted pages, no documents, no

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:33.480
 waiting.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.650
 Choose your bank, type your 10 digit

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.000
 account number and verify.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.970
 Paystack checks it against the bank and

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:45.070
 sends back the name on the account before

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:46.200
 you commit.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.940
 If that name is not yours, you have just

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:52.040
 caught a wrong digit before a single

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.680
 payout went anywhere.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:58.520
 Connect, and that is it. Bank connected.

